    "result_text": "Done. The build succeeds and the test suite is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `checkDigit` response field is a derived value over `customerCode`, so it belongs with the other derived owner fields (`membershipNumber`, `identityKey`, etc.) that the response mapper computes.\n\n1. **`model/CheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility helper defining the Luhn algorithm in one place: fold the digit characters of a code right-to-left (rightmost doubled), skipping non-digits, and return the digit that rounds the sum up to the next multiple of ten. This mirrors the existing `OwnerIdentity`/`Locality` model-helper pattern rather than inlining the math into the mapper.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", \u2026)` and a `checkDigit(owner)` default method that delegates to `CheckDigit.luhn(...)`, returning `null` when the customer code is unset (consistent with how `membershipNumber` guards on nulls).\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the `checkDigit` property on the Owner schema (int32, 0\u20139, read-only) so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` test recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact `checkDigit`, and it passes.",
